WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.937
(playful music)

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:06.330
- Why not?

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:07.840
- [Narrator] This is Timothy Hammond,

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.380
a Houston-based gardener
who knows his arugula.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.320
- I'm an urban gardener and educator

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.720
and one thing I know is that
you'll never find anybody

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.280
in this world who loves
gardening more than I do.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.230
- [Narrator] So what better person

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:19.320
to help us test this.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.061
The Rise Gardens Family Garden.

00:00:22.061 --> 00:00:24.644
(lively music)

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:29.660
As people spent more time
at home during the pandemic,

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:31.320
demand has surged for activities,

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:34.820
like cooking, home improvement
and yes, gardening.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.040
So that's why we're testing
the Rise Gardens Smart Garden.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.863
It's an indoor smart garden
that uses hydroponics.

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:44.530
It allows you to grow up to 12 vegetables

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:45.770
and herbs per shelf

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:48.720
using a self-watering
system and grow lights.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.840
- I'm interested to see if this garden,

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.950
this Rise Garden produces better

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.930
than some plants that I'm gonna start

00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:59.020
at the same time outside.

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:01.520
- [Narrator] So why did
we pick this smart garden?

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:02.970
A few reasons.

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:05.940
This smart garden is designed
for small indoor spaces

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.830
and claims to grow larger vegetables,

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:10.110
not just herbs and leafy greens.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:11.670
It's also adjustable.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:13.800
The modular system lets you add shelves up

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.560
to three different growing levels.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.740
It's Wi-Fi enabled with a connected app

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:19.160
so you can control the light,

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:21.220
water and nutrient levels

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:23.050
and get reminder alerts and updates.

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:24.270
- So I've never really thought

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:27.050
about bringing my gardening inside.

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:28.770
Now, they promised that you will be able

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:32.270
to recreate outside harvest inside.

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:33.790
- [Narrator] The Rise Garden systems come

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:38.380
in three sizes, ranging in
price from $549 to $949.

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:43.500
There's also a smaller
personal garden for $279.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:47.933
The one Timothy is testing
is $749 but is it worth it?

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:50.380
Timothy has more than four weeks

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:51.810
to test out this smart garden

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:53.620
and give us his final review.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:54.730
- Here we are

00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:59.331
and I guess now it's
time to start gardening.

00:01:59.331 --> 00:02:02.530
(playful music)

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:04.640
- [Narrator] Timothy first
assessed the planting process

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:05.473
with the garden.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:09.650
- Arugula should sprout
in five days they say.

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:11.710
Now, some of these seed cups say

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:14.100
that these things like the lettuce

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.160
or the arugula or the basil

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:19.490
will take anywhere from five
to eight days to sprout.

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:20.400
- [Narrator] Then he planted

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.550
his own seeds outside to compare.

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:25.460
- Let's go ahead and pot up some basil,

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:27.860
some arugula and some lettuce.

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:29.000
So I can tell you,

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.630
one of the benefits of
using that Rise Garden

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.840
is you don't have to deal
with this intense heat,

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:36.099
so you're probably able to grow things,

00:02:36.099 --> 00:02:38.643
a variety of things year round.

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:42.170
Now we'll set these in a shaded area

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:44.280
and we'll check back in about a week or so

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.670
to see if these sprouted at the same time

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:48.262
as our Rise Garden.

00:02:48.262 --> 00:02:50.929
(playful music)

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:53.720
- [Narrator] Next, he
gauged how easy the garden

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:55.050
is to maintain.

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:57.450
- I think the flashing
light means it's working.

00:02:58.470 --> 00:02:59.660
(playful music)

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:01.943
Ha, your garden is connected.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:05.190
Look at the lights dimming.

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:06.773
It's testing the lights.

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:10.490
The fact that it sends
me alerts through an app

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:11.510
is pretty cool.

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:13.610
I mean, it makes it a lot easier

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:15.900
to remember things
involved with the garden

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:17.860
and that's one thing that we really want

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:21.040
is to make sure that we
are staying on top of it

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.620
and the app helps you stay
on top of the gardening.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.660
So today we're gonna
do a reservoir change,

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:27.530
change the water out in the reservoir

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:29.540
because you can check the water level.

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:31.580
Now we're down to two.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.530
And then we're actually gonna throw in,

00:03:34.616 --> 00:03:36.353
I'm gonna throw in some
of these nutrients here.

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:39.030
I'm excited.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.783
Check out the arugula taking off.

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:44.425
Okay.

00:03:44.425 --> 00:03:46.560
Onc you put the nutrients in,

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.350
I think it was about a week and a half in,

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:51.340
about 10 days in once
I put the nutrients in,

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:53.588
then stuff really started taking off.

00:03:53.588 --> 00:03:56.330
(playful music)

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:57.590
- [Narrator] Finally, he compared

00:03:57.590 --> 00:03:59.330
how the same seeds grew outside

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:01.030
in comparison to the smart garden.

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:03.160
- This is day two with the Rise Garden

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:04.900
and I wanted to show you that the seeds

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:07.750
that we planted outside
have already sprouted.

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:09.773
We already have some arugula sprouting.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:14.703
While the Rise Garden
has still not sprouted.

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:20.520
Nothing beats the sun and Mother Nature.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:25.490
We have some basil sprouting
in the nursery up here,

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:26.783
which is pretty cool.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.950
But let's take a look at
the rest of the garden.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:32.820
See, we have basil sprouting here also.

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:34.810
That's on the top shelf.

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:36.630
- [Narrator] So how did the outdoor seeds

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:38.020
ultimately compare?

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:40.080
- So as you can see here,

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.120
the ones that we had outside,

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:44.270
they have to deal with the elements.

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:46.510
While they were the first to sprout,

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:49.320
they quickly stalled and slowed down

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:51.410
once that 100-degree weather,

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:54.970
that 100-degree Houston
weather came into account.

00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:58.460
- [Narrator] So what's Timothy's
final take after 25 days?

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:01.010
- So when it comes to this
Rise Garden Smart Garden,

00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:03.170
I'd give it a four out of five.

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:06.800
First, I love how well
it grows leafy greens.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:09.260
I love how simple it is to use.

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:12.820
I love the app keeping
up with when I planted

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:16.610
and when I need to do water
changes and things like that.

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:19.540
But a few things that I
don't like with the system,

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:23.210
first, I don't like that the
shelves are not adjustable.

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:25.830
Meaning I have to put my
taller plants on the bottom

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:29.930
and also, they get less
light down on the bottom.

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:34.370
Second, it's not easy to
clean out the reservoir

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:36.120
and empty and change the water

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:38.420
whenever it's time for water changes.

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:40.750
And third thing is the price.

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:43.033
At over $700,

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.600
that's a little too steep for me

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:49.430
but I love what this garden is able to do.

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:50.490
And I love the fact

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:53.560
that you could grow year
round with this thing.

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:55.680
- [Narrator] A Rise Garden
spokesman said the purpose

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:56.570
of the shelf height

00:05:56.570 --> 00:05:59.240
is to keep the structure
simple and refined.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:02.140
They're also working on
improving the cleaning process.

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:04.230
He added, "While the
price point is quite high

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:05.580
for a hobby like gardening,

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:07.920
we really wanted to not
cut corners on materials

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:09.780
and technology in order to allow people

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:12.450
to go from a fun hobby
to truly replacing items

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:13.770
on their grocery list."

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:15.290
- And just like that,

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:17.723
you have a nice bowl of
salad greens right here.

00:06:19.898 --> 00:06:22.565
(playful music)

